{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>who shall rise up after them</b> — ר\"ת (notarikon of) אחאב, ירבעם, מנשה: Ahab, Jeroboam, Manasseh, who wickedened with idolatry more than all of them." "<b>חלה</b> Two times in the Masorah: here, and the other: וכהצר לו חלה את פני ה' וגומר ונעתר לו. And we expound ויחתר לו — teaches that HaShem bored a bore beneath the Throne of Glory and received him in repentance. And that is: just as חלה here is an expression of breaking in the earth, so too חלה by Manasseh is an expression of boring, that a breach was made for him in the firmament."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:11:02.530877518Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}